discretion, to effect a reverse stock split or any action that requires stockholder approval, may not be adequate to cure compliance with the continued listing standards or that we may otherwise
fail to meet the NYSE&#146;s continued listing standards; and the risk that we may not obtain required stockholder approval of the proposal authorizing our board of directors, in their discretion, to effect a reverse stock split or any other action
intended to cure compliance with the NYSE&#146;s continued listing standards, and the other factors, risks and uncertainties included in our Annual Report on Form <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">10-K</FONT> for the fiscal year ended
December&nbsp;31, 2023, as such factors may be updated from time to time in our other filings with the Securities and Exchange Commission (the &#147;SEC&#148;), accessible on the SEC&#146;s website at www.sec.gov and the Investor Relations section
of our website at www.virgingalactic.com, which could cause our actual results to differ materially from those indicated by the forward-looking statements made in this press release. Any such forward-looking statements represent management&#146;s
